 - Answer MCP form elicitation requests (`elicitation/create`) with a dialog. Dismissing the dialog, or having no screen, cancels the request and never accepts it. URL mode is refused.
 - The task tool description now lists your model roles as `@role` and tells agents to pass the role when you name a model or tier such as "haiku", instead of guessing a model version. When the agent cannot tell which model you mean, it asks with the `ask` tool.
 - A task item's `model` can be a price tier, `$` to `$$$$`, instead of a role. Tiers are quarters of the price across all loaded chat models. A tier picks the configured role in that tier, or the nearest one, and the role you use most wins a tie. The usage weighting reads `stats.db` and counts the exact model most, then its family, then its provider. The task description shows each role's tier, and the judge that routes calls without `model` weighs price and usage too. `$$$$` is treated as very rare.
-- Each row in the pinned subagent shelf now ends with that subagent's total tokens, cache reads included, and its API cost, for example `1.4M tok · $0.42`. Cost is left out while it is zero, and a row too narrow for both drops the usage instead of the title. Subagent progress now reports `cacheReadTokens`.
+- Each row in the pinned subagent shelf now ends with that subagent's counter: elapsed time, total tokens (cache reads included) and API cost, for example `2m5s · 1.4M tok · $0.42`, each figure in its own theme colour (time and cost run hotter as they grow) with muted dots between them. The elapsed time shows from the first second and keeps counting while the subagent makes no progress, such as during a long rate-limit wait. Cost is left out while it is zero, and a row too narrow for the whole counter shortens the description first instead of dropping the counter. Subagent progress now reports `cacheReadTokens`.
+- The `Background job completed` line of a finished task job now shows the subagent's total tokens and cost beside the elapsed time, for example `(8m3s · 11M tok · $2.25)`, coloured like the shelf counter. A job that reports no usage keeps its plain duration.
 - Change a running subagent's model without restarting it: `write proc://<agentId>/model` with a configured role such as `@haiku` or one exact `provider/model-id[:level]` switches a subagent you spawned from its next model request, keeping its context. It takes the same approval as a task `model` (`task.perCallModel`, your grants, `task.perCallModelAllow`, `task.maxEffort`) and refuses a finished, unknown or foreign agent. The task description tells the agent to use it when you name a model or tier for a running agent.
 - `/switch <model>` and the model picker, used inside a subagent's view, now switch that subagent at its next model request instead of in the middle of the one in flight, and they work on a worker started with a per-call `model`, which used to fail its next request because the model was outside its grants. `/switch` resolves its selector in the viewed session. A notice in the subagent's view reports the switch when it lands, and a per-call worker revives on the model it last ran on.
 
@@ -21,6 +22,11 @@
 
 - `omp update` and the startup update check now use the latest stable release of the fork's GitHub repository (`kierandrewett/omp`, versions like `18.14.2-fork.1`): the `omp-linux-x64` asset is checked against `SHA256SUMS.txt` before it replaces the running binary, and the previous binary is restored if the new one fails version verification. `PI_BUILD_URL` and the upstream npm registry are no longer consulted, and npm, bun, Homebrew, mise and Nix installs are not updated from here.
 
+### Fixed
+
+- Fixed a lone `.` or `c` typed into a focused subagent that was still running, or waiting out a retry back-off, printing `Agent is already processing` as an error. The shortcut now queues as a steering message like any other text; the continue shortcut itself only restarts an idle agent.
+- Fixed a session wedged for days by a 429 carrying a huge retry hint, such as a 39-hour `retry-after-ms`: with `retry.waitForUsageReset` on it slept the whole wait while reporting busy, so `.` was refused and steers never landed. A wait past 24 hours now ends the retry (`auto_retry_end` with the error) and leaves the session idle. A 429 whose hint is past `retry.maxDelayMs` but is not a usage limit now blocks the failing credential until that hint and retries on a free sibling credential at once.
+
